        "id": 1003247
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-26T12:24:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a write into a non-checksum protected portion of the packet - ie. there is no accompanying checksum update that will cancel out this write.\n\nAs such this flag needs to be BPF_F_RECOMPUTE_CSUM and not 0,\notherwise we risk corrupting skb-\u003ecsum in the CHECKSUM_COMPLETE case.\n\nNote: this is very very subtle.\nTheoretically CHECKSUM_COMPLETE cannot even happen on transmit... unless\nwe\u0027re forwarding packets received from a rxcsum offload capable nic that delivers packets with CHECKSUM_COMPLETE set (not all nics do).\n\n(note that this is specific to writes to IPv6 header -- IPv4 header writes by virtue of the ipv4 header checksum updates does not need the flag)\n\nI spent hours getting to the bottom of this a year+ ago, and I\u0027m now just reading from my notes.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 167,
        "startChar": 87,
        "endLine": 167,
        "endChar": 88
      },
      "revId": "adf2d9560cb5c414c4645ca30dc4024f521063ba",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
